{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Destination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a plain sink: ","type":"text"},{"code":"deliver(to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" hands it each batch of records. Traffluent ships a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"few, each in a module of its own, so an app links only the ones it uses.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Logs and traces","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Logs-and-traces"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To see events beside your logs or traces, deliver to ","type":"text"},{"code":"LoggerDestination(logger:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") or ","type":"text"},{"code":"SpanEventDestination(tracer:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Only apps that use swift-log or swift-distributed-tracing this way link them. A span event joins","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the span that was active when the event was tracked, even if delivery runs later.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"A server","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"A-server"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To send batches to a server, deliver to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination(endpoint:headerFields:encoder:)"},{"text":" (module","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"text":"). It posts each batch as one request whose body is what your ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BatchEncoder"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes for it, so events need no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" conformance and the wire format is yours. A failed send","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is logged and dropped, without holding up the other destinations. It sends with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"text":" by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default, or through any ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPTransport"},{"text":" you pass as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transport:"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The bootstrapped tracing instrument, or the one you pass as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"instrument:"},{"type":"text","text":", injects the trace"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context of the batch’s first record into the request’s header fields, so a server that extracts it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"joins the request to the app’s trace. The encoder’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"type":"text","text":" always wins, and with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instrument bootstrapped no header is added. Only the first record’s context travels in the header"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fields; write each record’s context into the body if the server needs it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to a self-hosted TraffluentCollector, give "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder(plan:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":") as its encoder, and the collector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API key as an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Authorization: Bearer"},{"type":"text","text":" header field. It writes the collector’s ingest format: each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record’s identifier (which a redelivered record keeps), its name, timestamp and redelivery marker,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its properties read through the event’s schema in your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":", and its standard context and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trace context. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is sent only while the record reveals it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the rest of its batch is sent."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"That happens when the plan has no schema for the record’s event at its version (an event the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library tracks, such as "},{"code":"SessionStarted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", that the plan doesn’t list), when the event isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"BinaryCodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or when a value has no JSON form, such as a NaN. The encoder logs each skipped"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record at error level, and "},{"code":"batch(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s. A batch with no record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the encoder can write sends nothing."}]},{"text":"Memory","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Memory"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To read what was tracked inside the app, deliver to an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InMemoryDestination"},{"text":" as well (module","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations"},{"text":"): for an event inspector in a debug build, a recent-activity view, a SwiftUI","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"preview, or a test of what your code tracks. It keeps the newest 1,000 records, or as many as you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pass as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity:"},{"text":", dropping the oldest across batches; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"InMemoryDestination.unbounded()"},{"text":" keeps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every one. Read it with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events(of: SignedUp.self)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"records"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batches"},{"text":", or wait on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deliveries"},{"text":", which announces each batch to one reader.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Sensitive values and call sites","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Sensitive-values-and-call-sites"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A property that destinations shouldn’t see unless they must is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value. A destination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads it only through the record, with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reveal(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and printing or mirroring it shows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<redacted>"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"redactingSensitiveValues()"},{"type":"text","text":" makes a destination’s records reveal nothing, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"droppingCallSite()"},{"type":"text","text":" removes their call sites. Every other destination receives both:"}]},{"code":["struct SignedIn: Event {","    var email: Sensitive<String>","}","","let backend = InMemoryDestination()","let vendor = InMemoryDestination()","let tracker = Tracker()","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(","    to: backend,","    vendor.redactingSensitiveValues().droppingCallSite()",")","tracker.track(SignedIn(email: Sensitive(\"ada@example.com\")))","await tracker.finish()","try await delivery.execute()","let event = backend.events(of: SignedIn.self)[0]","let email = backend.records[0].reveal(event.email)    \/\/ \"ada@example.com\"","let redacted = vendor.records[0].reveal(event.email)  \/\/ nil","let callSite = vendor.records[0].sourceLocation       \/\/ nil"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"accepting(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" narrows a destination to the consent categories it serves ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChoosingDestinations","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Deliver events to your logs, your traces, a server or memory, and decide what each destination may see."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Choosing Destinations"},"kind":"article","references":{"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations":{"url":"\/documentation\/destinations","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations","type":"topic","title":"Destinations","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"topic","title":"HTTPDestinations","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ConsentGating":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/consentgating","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Deliver an event only once the user grants the purpose it is collected for."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ConsentGating","type":"topic","title":"Consent Gating","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://CollectorEncoding/documentation/CollectorEncoding":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"CollectorEncoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/collectorencoding","kind":"symbol"},"doc://TracingDestinations/documentation/TracingDestinations":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/tracingdestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/documentation\/TracingDestinations","kind":"symbol","title":"TracingDestinations","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingEvents":{"role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Tracking Events","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingEvents","abstract":[{"text":"Track typed events with a tracker, then deliver them in batches to any number of destinations.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingevents","kind":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingFromViews":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give views the tracker the way each framework passes values down, and let modifiers and controls track what views do."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","type":"topic","title":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TestingWhatYouTrack":{"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a test’s body with a fresh tracker and check the events it tracked."}],"title":"Testing What Your Code Tracks","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TestingWhatYouTrack","kind":"article"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Vendor-neutral analytics for Swift: typed events, tracked by a tracker and delivered in batches to any number of destinations."}],"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent","type":"topic","title":"Traffluent","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://LoggingDestinations/documentation/LoggingDestinations":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","title":"LoggingDestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoggingDestinations\/documentation\/LoggingDestinations","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/loggingdestinations","kind":"symbol"}}}